@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+# smallpt for the browser
+
+Kevin Beason's [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/), compiled from C++ to WebAssembly with Emscripten. The original source and MIT license are retained here. `smallpt.cpp` preserves the original radiance integrator and adds a C interface for progressive accumulation, pixel access, and sphere colors.
+
+- `npm run build:wasm` rebuilds `public/wasm/smallpt.js` and `smallpt.wasm` (requires `emcc`). Compiled assets are committed, so normal app builds do not need Emscripten.
+- `node scripts/check-wasm.mjs` checks real rendered pixels and sphere color changes in Node.
+- `npm run build` builds the Astro app; `npm run dev -- --host 0.0.0.0` starts development.
+- The playground is available at `/` and `/index.html`.
+
+The module runs in a dedicated module worker. Each pass traces four camera samples per pixel with the original 2×2 tent filter. Rows are batched for progress updates; the interface can stop a render by terminating the worker. Randomize changes both sphere reflectance colors and starts a new render. The original mirror and glass material types are preserved. The canvas supports PNG export and fullscreen.
+
+`public/images/smallpt-preview.png` is a 256-spp native render of the same C++ implementation, displayed while the first WebAssembly pass loads. All subsequent frames are computed on the device. This preview can be reproduced with `g++ renderer/smallpt.cpp -O3 -DNATIVE_PREVIEW -o /tmp/smallpt-preview`; running the binary writes a 640×480 raw RGBA buffer to `/tmp/smallpt.rgba` for PNG conversion.
